WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.836
Paul: 
Be me for a second. Would you
trust you?

00:00:03.128 --> 00:00:03.837
The answer is no.

00:00:04.296 --> 00:00:05.005
-Ahh!
-(Screaming)

00:00:05.881 --> 00:00:07.674
Well, you didn’t let me be you. 

00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:08.300
Here.

00:00:09.343 --> 00:00:13.347
Jimmy, sorry for always being so
hard on ya, it’s only cause I
love ya.

00:00:14.223 --> 00:00:15.140
 I don’t talk like that.

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:18.352
When Harrison said that he would
do it 

00:00:18.352 --> 00:00:21.480
and I saw the announcement
I thought it was a practical
joke.

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:25.776
It seemed unreal that you wanted
to do this show with me.

00:00:25.776 --> 00:00:27.069
Oh, man, come on. 

00:00:27.069 --> 00:00:32.324
No, it’s really true and I’m
sure at some point, this is my
every day.

00:00:32.574 --> 00:00:36.828
♪I'm on the pursuit of
happiness, and I know♪

00:00:36.828 --> 00:00:37.829
Sit down, Jimmy.

00:00:37.829 --> 00:00:39.498
If I sit down, I’m going to feel
like I’m in trouble.

00:00:39.498 --> 00:00:40.624
You are in trouble!

00:00:40.958 --> 00:00:45.295
They wanted John Wayne but they
were disappointed to hear about
his demise.

00:00:45.295 --> 00:00:46.213
(Laughing)

00:00:46.213 --> 00:00:49.091
Do you know who the most
important person in your life is
right now?

00:00:49.091 --> 00:00:49.675
You.

00:00:49.675 --> 00:00:52.469
No, you sh..head, your daughter!

00:00:52.469 --> 00:00:53.720
Right, that’s what I meant.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:54.638
I’m second.

00:00:55.222 --> 00:00:55.973
Okay.

00:00:56.348 --> 00:00:59.309
In all seriousness, I’ve always
admired his work.

00:00:59.309 --> 00:01:05.774
The writing is fantastic and the
relationship is to me really
funny and interesting.

00:01:05.774 --> 00:01:07.651
He doesn’t think so but I do.

00:01:07.651 --> 00:01:08.610
(Laughing)

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:09.695
Could we talk?

00:01:09.695 --> 00:01:11.280
I don’t need another lecture.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:12.114
It’s about Gabby.

00:01:12.114 --> 00:01:15.075
Oh, I was kinda looking forward
to a fight.

00:01:15.367 --> 00:01:16.243
Yeah, I could tell.

00:01:16.243 --> 00:01:19.997
These two guys, they have a
mentor-mentee relationship,

00:01:19.997 --> 00:01:22.541
but I think it’s also a
surrogate father-son
relationship.

00:01:22.541 --> 00:01:25.502
Jimmy desperately wants Paul’s
approval.

00:01:25.502 --> 00:01:26.712
You just said you love me.

00:01:26.712 --> 00:01:27.838
No, I did not!

00:01:27.838 --> 00:01:29.172
Well, it sounded like you did. 

00:01:29.172 --> 00:01:30.382
Oh...

00:01:30.799 --> 00:01:34.469
Jason Segel:
I think Paul has a really
complicated relationship with his kids

00:01:34.469 --> 00:01:41.184
and sees Jimmy as potentially a
son so the show is all about
lines being blurred 

00:01:41.184 --> 00:01:44.730
and I think that the Paul-Jimmy
relationship is a real example
of that.

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:46.690
I’ve known you for years, I’ve
never met your daughter.

00:01:46.690 --> 00:01:47.858
Yeah, what is she like?

00:01:47.858 --> 00:01:49.484
She lives in Connecticut.

00:01:51.653 --> 00:01:54.614
Wow. It’s like she’s in the
room.

00:01:55.741 --> 00:02:01.830
The character that Jason plays
is complex and uh, visceral and
exciting.

00:02:02.331 --> 00:02:04.750
Harrison Ford:
The relationship comes from the
writers

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:09.504
but there also is a personal
relationship that, that fuels
me.

00:02:10.505 --> 00:02:11.673
Who knows how you grieve?

00:02:11.673 --> 00:02:13.175
You haven’t even begun.

00:02:13.175 --> 00:02:14.217
What are you talking about?

00:02:14.217 --> 00:02:16.011
I’ve been grieving for a year

00:02:16.011 --> 00:02:18.430
No, you’ve been numbing.

00:02:19.348 --> 00:02:20.932
Paul:
I’m worried about you.

00:02:21.433 --> 00:02:26.104
Harrison Ford:
It’s the kind of material where
I don’t know if from one moment to the next

00:02:26.104 --> 00:02:28.023
whether I'm going to laugh or
cry.

00:02:28.190 --> 00:02:31.193
I feel enormously lucky to
just be part of this thing.

00:02:31.193 --> 00:02:31.818
Jason Segel:
Same.

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:34.613
Harrison Ford
And, I think it’s good for
people to laugh.

00:02:34.613 --> 00:02:36.573
You should see Harrison Ford do
comedy.

00:02:36.573 --> 00:02:37.657
Not today.

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:38.658
No, not today.

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:39.284
(Laughing)

00:02:39.284 --> 00:02:41.244
Do you know what percentage of
yourself is actually made of
water?

00:02:41.244 --> 00:02:43.538
I know what percentage of me
doesn’t give a sh..

00:02:43.538 --> 00:02:45.332
Ok, well, that’s the dehydration
talking.

